WEBVTT

1
00:51:07.010 --> 00:51:12.210
Are there any guests in Open Church today? Are there people here for the first time in Open Church today?

2
00:51:12.210 --> 00:51:19.010
Give a wave if you are here today... There we have some people. Can we have a round of applause for our guests, please?

3
00:51:24.410 --> 00:51:28.010
You are very welcome. Hallelujah.

4
00:51:32.510 --> 00:51:33.510
Is everyone happy?

5
00:51:34.510 --> 00:51:38.510
For the joy of the Lord is my strength. Amen.

6
00:51:39.510 --> 00:51:40.510
Hallelujah.

7
00:51:41.510 --> 00:51:44.510
I am enjoying looking at everyone. You all look good like this.

8
00:51:45.510 --> 00:51:47.510
Me too, yes. I already knew that.

9
00:51:48.510 --> 00:51:49.510
Praise God.

10
00:51:50.510 --> 00:51:58.510
Hallelujah. As you know, we are in a thematic year called Build a House.

11
00:51:59.510 --> 00:52:09.510
And initially, we are teaching as a church about the fact that we together are the temples of the Holy Spirit...

12
00:52:09.510 --> 00:52:18.510
You are a temple of the Holy Spirit, but together we build a spiritual temple with spiritual sacrifices that God is pleased with.

13
00:52:18.510 --> 00:52:31.510
Again, to repeat what I just said. We build nothing without Jesus. He established the kingdom on earth.

14
00:52:32.510 --> 00:52:39.510
It is all up to Him. The only thing we can do is join Him. And then build together with Jesus.

15
00:52:40.510 --> 00:52:54.510
And 2024 is the year Build a House. We have started with the planning and organization and involving all of us in the fact that we are also going to build a new building.

16
00:52:54.510 --> 00:52:57.510
A new church building. You know this, right?

17
00:52:58.510 --> 00:53:06.510
In two weeks, we will have a collection about this together. It is important, we have discussed this with the team, it is important that you regularly...

18
00:53:06.510 --> 00:53:16.510
...specify well that you say and communicate to the church, this collection goes there. So that we all know what we are giving to.

19
00:53:16.510 --> 00:53:25.510
So last week, Bram said, this collection goes to the daily operations of Open Church.

20
00:53:25.510 --> 00:53:32.510
The mortgage we pay, the salaries we pay, the teams that have various costs needed to operate.

21
00:53:32.510 --> 00:53:41.510
So it is very important to participate together, financially, in the daily workings of this church. The daily matters.

22
00:53:41.510 --> 00:53:51.510
But we also collected for Tycoon Global, for example. I always say Tycoon Israel, because I know it goes to Israel.

23
00:53:51.510 --> 00:54:03.510
As a church, we pray for Israel, we pray for the Christians in Israel, and we also give money to the Messianic Christians, to the Messianic Jews in Israel.

24
00:54:03.510 --> 00:54:15.510
So that they can evangelize to the Jews in Israel who do not yet know Jesus. For the Jews in Israel, it is important that they accept Jesus as Messiah.

25
00:54:15.510 --> 00:54:26.510
Can I get an amen on that? And this work is a work that we as Gentile Christians, the word Gentile meaning all people who are not Jews.

26
00:54:26.510 --> 00:54:34.510
This is an important work for us. Why? Because the Bible commands us to do so. That it is important for us.

27
00:54:34.510 --> 00:54:40.510
Paul says in the letter to the Romans that it is important for the Gentiles to have love for the Jews.

28
00:54:40.510 --> 00:54:45.510
And he tells the Jews that it is important to have love for the Gentiles.

29
00:54:45.510 --> 00:54:50.510
When these two come together in unity, that is the perfection of the bride of Christ.

30
00:54:50.510 --> 00:55:02.510
And how can we show our love for our brothers and sisters in Israel? By supporting them in love, in prayer, and with money. Amen.

31
00:55:02.510 --> 00:55:10.510
And so we had, when was it? One or two weeks ago, two weeks ago we collected for Ticon Global.

32
00:55:10.510 --> 00:55:18.510
And we raised five thousand euros together and we also transferred five thousand euros to Israel this week.

33
00:55:18.510 --> 00:55:23.510
And I actually think that deserves a round of applause. Yes, I think that’s wonderful.

34
00:55:24.510 --> 00:55:34.510
Bram already said last week, well, ultimately with these kinds of amounts, how am I going to say that?

35
00:55:34.510 --> 00:55:45.510
Paul sometimes writes in his letters in the New Testament, that he says to the church, I praise you, I think you are wonderful for being so generous.

36
00:55:46.510 --> 00:55:50.510
Do you understand? So I want to say this to us as a church. I just think it’s wonderful.

37
00:55:50.510 --> 00:56:00.510
Not to be proud of ourselves, that we just look how good we are, but as a church you can be happy that you can also be generous together.

38
00:56:00.510 --> 00:56:08.510
And that you stand for something together and that you can tackle things together and that you can build the kingdom of God together in actions.

39
00:56:08.510 --> 00:56:15.510
That can be in Christ, in humility in Christ you can be very happy with that and even proud of it.

40
00:56:15.510 --> 00:56:22.510
Do you understand what I mean? Pride can be a sin, but being proud of something that you can be as a church is not necessarily a sin.

41
00:56:22.510 --> 00:56:32.510
Do you understand my balance? And so I just want to say, I find it amazing that we as a little church in the Kempen are raising such amounts for such wonderful works.

42
00:56:32.510 --> 00:56:37.510
So I just want to say on behalf of everyone, thank you all very much.

43
00:56:37.510 --> 00:56:45.510
And the other thing I want to say is about that construction, about that construction project we have started.

44
00:56:45.510 --> 00:57:01.510
So actually somewhere in, okay, just to say, last year July somewhere it started to dawn that in the prayer and in the revelation it came forward that God indicates

45
00:57:01.510 --> 00:57:07.510
it is time to prepare for the construction of a new church building.

46
00:57:07.510 --> 00:57:19.510
And then you start to pray, so if you believe you are picking something up from God in prayer and if you believe you are receiving a signal, then you always, that's a tip, you pray the following.

47
00:57:19.510 --> 00:57:23.510
Then you say, Lord if this is you, let it be shown, give confirmations.

48
00:57:23.510 --> 00:57:29.510
You see this very often in the Bible. If you believe you are picking something up from God, just ask for confirmations.

49
00:57:29.510 --> 00:57:35.510
Just say, Lord are you the one speaking here? Would you show that you are? Would you open doors?

50
00:57:35.510 --> 00:57:40.510
That is a very nice type of prayer. Would you open doors, Lord? Would you show that you are?

51
00:57:40.510 --> 00:57:45.510
Would you give favor and grace? Would you give the green light? You understand the kind of prayer I mean here.

52
00:57:45.510 --> 00:57:51.510
And God has really clearly shown from that moment on and you know the stories also explained since Vision Sunday.

53
00:57:51.510 --> 00:57:57.510
You know the stories that pieces of land came to us, literally, as just an offer to be able to buy.

54
00:57:57.510 --> 00:58:03.510
And so God showed, through favor, that God in this project really says, this is my will.

55
00:58:03.510 --> 00:58:06.510
For it is not our will, but let His will be done. Amen.

56
00:58:06.510 --> 00:58:15.510
And so from about January, the launch of this project, you also go with an architect and with a construction team

57
00:58:15.510 --> 00:58:22.510
and with the city of Lommel, where God has placed us, we will be in communication to undertake this construction project.

58
00:58:22.510 --> 00:58:28.510
And I just want to give a little newsflash, which I find very cool. It is really a milestone that has been laid down.

59
00:58:28.510 --> 00:58:36.510
Last Friday we received an email from the architect and from the city of Lommel. We really received both within the hour.

60
00:58:36.510 --> 00:58:47.510
We got the go-ahead, not the permit itself, but the application for the permit has officially been launched with the city of Lommel.

61
00:58:47.510 --> 00:58:54.510
And that is a milestone. Why is this a milestone? It is a milestone because you have to deliver a lot of preparatory work,

62
00:58:54.510 --> 00:59:03.510
I am really talking about a lot of preparatory work, that you have to provide. And that is a process that you undertake together as church, city, and architect.

63
00:59:03.510 --> 00:59:11.510
And there are so many technicalities involved. Environment, spatial planning, legal matters are involved.

64
00:59:12.510 --> 00:59:19.510
So you have to tick off all sorts of things before you can even look at whether you will get a building permit.

65
00:59:19.510 --> 00:59:28.510
Well, that building permit was officially applied for last Friday. And I would like to pray for that, if you could all stand for a moment.

66
00:59:28.510 --> 00:59:42.510
I just want to pray for you, because you have to work and pray. You have to pray and work. That is the right combination.

67
00:59:43.510 --> 00:59:59.510
And they explained to us that when you apply for a building permit, you submit that to the city of Lommel and then there are 30 days for the city to review that building permit application.

68
00:59:59.510 --> 01:00:09.510
To check that all the information is correct. 30 days will then pass. After that, another 30 days will pass for, I don't know, something like that.

69
01:00:09.510 --> 01:00:16.510
And then 75 days will pass. 30 days, 30 days, 75 days.

70
01:00:16.510 --> 01:00:28.510
And during that time, everything will be checked by the city and the province. Then a yellow sign will be placed in the yard to inform the neighborhood that we are going to do this.

71
01:00:28.510 --> 01:00:37.510
And then complaints would be filed. Of course, no complaints will be filed. Amen. One amen. I thought so too.

72
01:00:37.510 --> 01:00:45.510
Because we will place an angel there with a fiery sword and we will pray that this does not happen.

73
01:00:45.510 --> 01:00:52.510
But seriously, shall we pray for this application? That is a good idea.

74
01:00:52.510 --> 01:01:02.510
Dear King Jesus, we thank you. We praise your holy name. We honor the name of Jesus, the risen Lord.

75
01:01:02.510 --> 01:01:09.510
To you be all glory and honor, forever and ever. But Father, we have also learned from the Word of God that we must always pray.

76
01:01:09.510 --> 01:01:15.510
Not my will, but your will be done. And in that same prayer, our Father in heaven,

77
01:01:15.510 --> 01:01:22.510
Your name be hallowed and let your kingdom come. Your will be done in heaven and on earth.

78
01:01:22.510 --> 01:01:31.510
Lord, over this project I want to pronounce a blessing together with my brothers and sisters in the room at this moment over this building permit application.

79
01:01:31.510 --> 01:01:41.510
Pray with me, look. I want to ask for a blessing for this building permit application, that there is protection over it in the name of Jesus.

80
01:01:41.510 --> 01:01:49.510
Lord, I want to pray that there is favor over it in the name of Jesus. Lord, that you will open doors here in the government.

81
01:01:49.510 --> 01:01:55.510
Then either the government of the city of Lommel and the province or even if it needs to go higher.

82
01:01:55.510 --> 01:02:05.510
Lord, I want to pray, Lord, that there will be favor. Favor with God and with people. Favor with officials and aldermen and mayors.

83
01:02:05.510 --> 01:02:14.510
Lord, that you will show the revelation of whether these people are saved or not. You give revelations to both the righteous and the unrighteous.

84
01:02:14.510 --> 01:02:19.510
Lord, and so I want to pray in Jesus' name, Lord, that your favor will rest on this project.

85
01:02:19.510 --> 01:02:26.510
Lord, that stamps will be placed, that approvals will come, that signatures will come.

86
01:02:26.510 --> 01:02:34.510
Lord, I also want to pray, Lord, that everything that could be opposed, Lord, that it will be removed in the name of Jesus.

87
01:02:34.510 --> 01:02:43.510
Lord, every complaint, every opposition, everything that Satan would want to throw against this church at all, but also against this project.

88
01:02:43.510 --> 01:02:52.510
Every discord, every objection, every ungodliness, I bind this and tie this in the mighty name of King Jesus.

89
01:02:52.510 --> 01:02:57.510
And so I say, Lord, help us, Lord, with this great project.

90
01:02:57.510 --> 01:03:00.510
Lord, for if you are for us, who can be against us?

91
01:03:00.510 --> 01:03:09.510
Lord, you are so great and so we bless this milestone, so we bless this building permit application in the mighty name of King Jesus.

92
01:03:09.510 --> 01:03:14.510
And we all say, Amen, Amen and Amen. Hallelujah.

93
01:03:17.510 --> 01:03:23.510
Here it says lastly, then I may invite Ruben to come and teach about the collections.

94
01:03:24.510 --> 01:03:32.510
Have you already signed up your son or daughter or spouse for the summer camp?

95
01:03:32.510 --> 01:03:39.510
I recently heard the score from Cindy, what was the score approximately of the number of registrations?

96
01:03:40.510 --> 01:03:42.510
Are you already at forty registrations?

97
01:03:43.510 --> 01:03:44.510
Men, you should be ashamed.

98
01:03:46.510 --> 01:03:48.510
I am at ten registrations, men.

99
01:03:48.510 --> 01:03:52.510
Last time it was the same, I don't know where that was, it was some kind of bottleneck.

100
01:03:52.510 --> 01:03:55.510
Last year I also thought, this is not going to happen.

101
01:03:55.510 --> 01:03:58.510
By the way, if we go with ten men, we will make it enjoyable.

102
01:03:58.510 --> 01:04:01.510
Because those ten men I saw, I find them the most fun.

103
01:04:03.510 --> 01:04:05.510
And everyone who joins is also the most fun to me.

104
01:04:05.510 --> 01:04:09.510
But please sign up, men. Let us know that you are coming.

105
01:04:09.510 --> 01:04:13.510
Question-free, from September 13 to 15 is Men's Camp.

106
01:04:13.510 --> 01:04:17.510
Friday, Saturday, and Sunday morning, and then we will drive together nicely to the church.

107
01:04:17.510 --> 01:04:21.510
Hallelujah, praise afterwards. But please, sign up.

108
01:04:21.510 --> 01:04:26.510
Because then we also know how many we need to register for everything and anything.

109
01:04:26.510 --> 01:04:29.510
But also sign up your teenagers for the teen camp.

110
01:04:29.510 --> 01:04:32.510
Sign up your children for the children's camp. Do it.

111
01:04:32.510 --> 01:04:34.510
If you have doubts, do it.

112
01:04:34.510 --> 01:04:38.510
And if you are sure that you are not going to do it, do it anyway.

113
01:04:38.510 --> 01:04:45.510
Because truly, the summer camps are also milestones in the lives of children and teenagers.

114
01:04:45.510 --> 01:04:47.510
And also of adult men.

115
01:04:47.510 --> 01:04:52.510
Really, it is liberating, it provides, it nourishes. It is just really amazing.

116
01:04:52.510 --> 01:04:54.510
So please, sign up.

117
01:04:54.510 --> 01:04:58.510
Ruben may invite you for the collection.

118
01:04:58.510 --> 01:04:59.510
Good morning.

119
01:05:08.510 --> 01:05:10.510
Good morning.

120
01:05:11.510 --> 01:05:17.510
Tim has already told a number of things about giving and about the collection.

121
01:05:17.510 --> 01:05:23.510
And I found it so beautiful that he said everything comes from him.

122
01:05:23.510 --> 01:05:27.510
Zero percent me, one hundred percent God.

123
01:05:27.510 --> 01:05:34.510
And exactly, what I had in my mind as a title, if you can write it that way, if a collection can have a title,

124
01:05:34.510 --> 01:05:39.510
is that we give because God gives.

125
01:05:40.510 --> 01:05:43.510
And as I started to think about that,

126
01:05:43.510 --> 01:05:47.510
when you stand here and you get to promote the collection, and that is what we do,

127
01:05:47.510 --> 01:05:51.510
to give to God, to give financially to God,

128
01:05:51.510 --> 01:05:54.510
that may not be as easy as it seems.

129
01:05:55.510 --> 01:05:58.510
And we do it every week anyway, why?

130
01:05:58.510 --> 01:06:01.510
Because God encourages us to give.

131
01:06:02.510 --> 01:06:03.510
Why?

132
01:06:03.510 --> 01:06:06.510
Because God himself is someone who gives.

133
01:06:07.510 --> 01:06:10.510
And as I look into the Word of God,

134
01:06:10.510 --> 01:06:16.510
and they are very basic Bible verses that I have shared today,

135
01:06:16.510 --> 01:06:20.510
and the first is John 3:16 and 17,

136
01:06:21.510 --> 01:06:25.510
it clearly states what God has done.

137
01:06:25.510 --> 01:06:28.510
For God loves people so much,

138
01:06:28.510 --> 01:06:33.510
that he has given his only Son to them.

139
01:06:34.510 --> 01:06:35.510
Given.

140
01:06:35.510 --> 01:06:39.510
And everyone who believes in him will not perish, but will have eternal life.

141
01:06:39.510 --> 01:06:43.510
Verse 17, I want to read that together always.

142
01:06:43.510 --> 01:06:45.510
And why is that?

143
01:06:45.510 --> 01:06:47.510
Because it truly belongs to it.

144
01:06:47.510 --> 01:06:51.510
God did not send his son into the world to condemn people,

145
01:06:51.510 --> 01:06:54.510
but to save people through him.

146
01:06:54.510 --> 01:06:56.510
That is what Jesus meant.

147
01:06:56.510 --> 01:07:01.510
And when you start to think, God is a giver.

148
01:07:01.510 --> 01:07:03.510
God gives.

149
01:07:03.510 --> 01:07:06.510
So he also asks us to give.

150
01:07:06.510 --> 01:07:08.510
But he does it himself too.

151
01:07:08.510 --> 01:07:12.510
And that is a reason that motivates us to give.

152
01:07:13.510 --> 01:07:15.510
Because God himself gives.

153
01:07:15.510 --> 01:07:19.510
And you see that in the Bible in many different places.

154
01:07:19.510 --> 01:07:22.510
When God asks something of us,

155
01:07:22.510 --> 01:07:26.510
that gives insight into his character, into his nature.

156
01:07:26.510 --> 01:07:29.510
When God asks us to give,

157
01:07:29.510 --> 01:07:32.510
that is his nature to give back.

158
01:07:32.510 --> 01:07:35.510
And when I read, and I have Galatians 5 verse 22 for that,

159
01:07:35.510 --> 01:07:37.510
he promises us the Holy Spirit.

160
01:07:37.510 --> 01:07:41.510
What God gives us, and what you yourself,

161
01:07:41.510 --> 01:07:45.510
when you decide to give in the kingdom of God you will experience,

162
01:07:45.510 --> 01:07:51.510
there is a disproportion between what you will give and what you will receive.

163
01:07:51.510 --> 01:07:58.510
And in this example what I give is a positive disproportion.

164
01:07:58.510 --> 01:08:01.510
Very often that has a negative connotation, disproportion.

165
01:08:01.510 --> 01:08:05.510
What God gives is disproportionate.

166
01:08:06.510 --> 01:08:10.510
Not in proportion to what we will give.

167
01:08:10.510 --> 01:08:13.510
And he gives us the Holy Spirit.

168
01:08:13.510 --> 01:08:15.510
And look at what he says.

169
01:08:15.510 --> 01:08:21.510
The fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace.

170
01:08:21.510 --> 01:08:24.510
People, those are the things we truly need.

171
01:08:24.510 --> 01:08:27.510
We do not need more money.

172
01:08:27.510 --> 01:08:30.510
We do not need more possessions.

173
01:08:30.510 --> 01:08:32.510
We need the fruit of the Spirit in our lives.

174
01:08:32.510 --> 01:08:35.510
And that is what he promises and what he gives.

175
01:08:35.510 --> 01:08:41.510
Patience, kindness, goodness, faith, helpfulness, and self-control.

176
01:08:41.510 --> 01:08:43.510
And I can encourage you.

177
01:08:43.510 --> 01:08:49.510
The Holy Spirit came into your life the moment you chose Jesus.

178
01:08:49.510 --> 01:08:52.510
In your heart, in your innermost being.

179
01:08:52.510 --> 01:08:56.510
And this fruit is what you will receive.

180
01:08:57.510 --> 01:08:58.510
Amen.

181
01:08:59.510 --> 01:09:02.510
I always find it good to pray.

182
01:09:02.510 --> 01:09:10.510
Heavenly Father, I want to thank you so much, Lord God, that we may be in your glory.

183
01:09:11.510 --> 01:09:13.510
Lord God, you are so good.

184
01:09:13.510 --> 01:09:23.510
Lord God, I am so grateful to you, Lord God, that we may read in your Word about a river that flows from our innermost being through your Spirit.

185
01:09:23.510 --> 01:09:30.510
And that we can heal and that the fruit of the Spirit is a result of what you have done for us.

186
01:09:31.510 --> 01:09:38.510
And I want to pray, Lord God, that we will come to understand and live according to the principles of your kingdom.

187
01:09:38.510 --> 01:09:41.510
We have sung a lot about it today. You sit on that throne.

188
01:09:42.510 --> 01:09:47.510
Lord God, we are part of another kingdom, where different principles apply.

189
01:09:48.510 --> 01:09:53.510
Lord God, where different rules apply, in which you have been the example in everything.

190
01:09:53.510 --> 01:09:58.510
Lord God, and I pray in your name, of course in your name, in the name of Jesus.

191
01:09:58.510 --> 01:10:00.510
In what other name could I pray?

192
01:10:00.510 --> 01:10:04.510
Lord God, because I know that there is power in that name.

193
01:10:04.510 --> 01:10:09.510
Lord God, and that through that name, Lord God, things will change.

194
01:10:09.510 --> 01:10:12.510
And I want to pray, Lord God, that we will be givers.

195
01:10:13.510 --> 01:10:16.510
Lord God, because you give back so much more than the things that truly matter.

196
01:10:17.510 --> 01:10:19.510
Lord God, I honor your name.

197
01:10:19.510 --> 01:10:24.510
And I thank you for this church and for the generosity that is in this church first.

198
01:10:25.510 --> 01:10:27.510
Lord God, you are good in everything, Lord God.

199
01:10:27.510 --> 01:10:29.510
And you love us, time and time again.

200
01:10:29.510 --> 01:10:31.510
In Jesus' name. Amen.

201
01:10:39.510 --> 01:10:41.510
Are you ready for the Word, people?

202
01:10:42.510 --> 01:10:44.510
Lastly, I want to ask one more thing.

203
01:10:46.510 --> 01:10:49.510
If you, no, I can put it better this way.

204
01:10:49.510 --> 01:10:51.510
In Open Church, we have live groups.

205
01:10:51.510 --> 01:10:56.510
And live groups are groups, friends who come together once a month.

206
01:10:56.510 --> 01:11:01.510
At the end of the month, the last Wednesday or in that last week of the month.

207
01:11:01.510 --> 01:11:03.510
The live groups come together.

208
01:11:03.510 --> 01:11:07.510
To talk together and to eat together and to make it cozy together.

209
01:11:07.510 --> 01:11:10.510
To study the Word of God together.

210
01:11:10.510 --> 01:11:14.510
About what the teaching of Open Church discussed that month.

211
01:11:15.510 --> 01:11:19.510
And I want to encourage everyone to go to a live group.

212
01:11:19.510 --> 01:11:21.510
I don't know if you already go to a live group.

213
01:11:21.510 --> 01:11:22.510
I don't know if you were aware of it.

214
01:11:22.510 --> 01:11:25.510
That's why it's important that I occasionally really say it.

215
01:11:25.510 --> 01:11:27.510
There are live groups in Open Church.

216
01:11:27.510 --> 01:11:28.510
And find one.

217
01:11:28.510 --> 01:11:31.510
One in the area where you live, nearby.

218
01:11:31.510 --> 01:11:35.510
That can be from Hasselt to the south towards Hasselt.

219
01:11:35.510 --> 01:11:37.510
I don't know where you live.

220
01:11:37.510 --> 01:11:38.510
But find one.

221
01:11:38.510 --> 01:11:40.510
Here sits Elle. Elle, give us a wave.

222
01:11:40.510 --> 01:11:43.510
Elle leads the live groups.

223
01:11:43.510 --> 01:11:46.510
If you want to join a live group, let us know.

224
01:11:46.510 --> 01:11:49.510
And we want to help you find a live group.

225
01:11:49.510 --> 01:11:50.510
Amen.

226
01:11:50.510 --> 01:11:51.510
Amen.

227
01:11:51.510 --> 01:11:54.510
Robert is coming to bring the Word of God.

228
01:11:54.510 --> 01:11:56.510
So I would appreciate it if we could stand one more time.

229
01:11:56.510 --> 01:11:59.510
Just to receive the Word of God as such.

230
01:11:59.510 --> 01:12:01.510
So that Robert can pray for the Word.

231
01:12:01.510 --> 01:12:04.510
And that we can receive this with reverence in our hearts.

232
01:12:04.510 --> 01:12:05.510
Hallelujah.

233
01:12:08.510 --> 01:12:10.510
Hallelujah, thank you Jesus.

234
01:12:11.510 --> 01:12:14.510
It has been all about you, Lord, this whole morning.

235
01:12:14.510 --> 01:12:16.510
And we want to meet you, Lord.

236
01:12:16.510 --> 01:12:18.510
We want to get to know you, Lord.

237
01:12:18.510 --> 01:12:19.510
More and more and more.

238
01:12:19.510 --> 01:12:21.510
Together as your congregation, Lord.

239
01:12:21.510 --> 01:12:24.510
So speak to us this morning, Lord.

240
01:12:24.510 --> 01:12:29.510
Help me, Lord, to bring your words as they are in your heart, Lord.

241
01:12:29.510 --> 01:12:32.510
And help us, Lord, to receive it.

242
01:12:32.510 --> 01:12:34.510
And to do something with it.

243
01:12:34.510 --> 01:12:35.510
In Jesus' name.

244
01:12:35.510 --> 01:12:36.510
Hallelujah.

245
01:12:36.510 --> 01:12:38.510
Thank you, worship team.

246
01:12:39.510 --> 01:12:43.510
I always love to worship Jesus together with you.

247
01:12:44.510 --> 01:12:46.510
For Jesus is so worthy of it.

248
01:12:46.510 --> 01:12:49.510
That we worship Him with all that is within us.

249
01:12:50.510 --> 01:12:55.510
Who is excited to dive into God's Word together this morning?

250
01:12:57.510 --> 01:13:01.510
Then you may grab the Bible right away.

251
01:13:01.510 --> 01:13:04.510
And we will go to Ephesians 1 verse 22.

252
01:13:08.510 --> 01:13:30.510
God has given Him, Jesus, power over everything.

253
01:13:30.510 --> 01:13:34.510
He has become ruler over all that exists.

254
01:13:34.510 --> 01:13:38.510
And He has made Jesus the head of the congregation.

255
01:13:39.510 --> 01:13:41.510
The congregation is His body.

256
01:13:41.510 --> 01:13:43.510
And the congregation is full of Him.

257
01:13:44.510 --> 01:13:50.510
He fills everything and everyone completely with Himself.

258
01:13:52.510 --> 01:13:57.510
He fills everything and everyone completely with Himself.

259
01:13:58.510 --> 01:14:00.510
How is it possible in God's name?

260
01:14:01.510 --> 01:14:11.510
We small insignificant humans and the great Almighty God who is pure love.

261
01:14:11.510 --> 01:14:14.510
He who loves many of us.

262
01:14:15.510 --> 01:14:17.510
He who has created everything.

263
01:14:17.510 --> 01:14:22.510
Fills us completely with Himself.

264
01:14:23.510 --> 01:14:24.510
Absurd.

265
01:14:26.510 --> 01:14:28.510
Just look around you.

266
01:14:29.510 --> 01:14:33.510
We are together the congregation of Christ.

267
01:14:33.510 --> 01:14:35.510
The body of Christ.

268
01:14:37.510 --> 01:14:40.510
And Jesus is the head.

269
01:14:40.510 --> 01:14:42.510
We are the body.

270
01:14:42.510 --> 01:14:44.510
Jesus is the head.

271
01:14:44.510 --> 01:14:46.510
He is the leader.

272
01:14:46.510 --> 01:14:50.510
He is the brains, the mind.

273
01:14:50.510 --> 01:14:53.510
He determines what happens.

274
01:14:53.510 --> 01:14:56.510
And we are His hands and His feet.

275
01:14:56.510 --> 01:14:59.510
And we carry out what He wants.

276
01:15:00.510 --> 01:15:08.510
And I find it so amazing how God speaks and leads us.

277
01:15:08.510 --> 01:15:13.510
This morning I am going to have this sermon with you about the body of Christ.

278
01:15:13.510 --> 01:15:15.510
We together.

279
01:15:15.510 --> 01:15:21.510
And this sermon that I find very nice that I may give this morning.

280
01:15:21.510 --> 01:15:25.510
Because it has been brewing in my heart for a year.

281
01:15:25.510 --> 01:15:30.510
And two weeks ago, during the worship evening on Monday,

282
01:15:30.510 --> 01:15:32.510
I was also a bit busy with that.

283
01:15:32.510 --> 01:15:37.510
Actually, the worship evening is not meant to receive, but to give.

284
01:15:37.510 --> 01:15:39.510
To worship God.

285
01:15:39.510 --> 01:15:42.510
But yes, that always goes a bit hand in hand.

286
01:15:42.510 --> 01:15:45.510
So I was talking to Jesus.

287
01:15:45.510 --> 01:15:54.510
And I said, Lord, would you show me something tonight that is still missing in what I have prepared.

288
01:15:55.510 --> 01:15:59.510
Five minutes later, Vanessa starts singing.

289
01:15:59.510 --> 01:16:01.510
Jesus is the head.

290
01:16:01.510 --> 01:16:04.510
Jesus is the leader.

291
01:16:04.510 --> 01:16:09.510
And as it sometimes goes on Monday, then a thousand times.

292
01:16:12.510 --> 01:16:15.510
Which I find completely fine and nice.

293
01:16:15.510 --> 01:16:19.510
And then I thought, yes, I must not forget,

294
01:16:19.510 --> 01:16:22.510
when we are going to talk about the body, which we are,

295
01:16:22.510 --> 01:16:27.510
to especially not skip over Jesus.

296
01:16:27.510 --> 01:16:29.510
I must not forget.

297
01:16:29.510 --> 01:16:34.510
And I also think it's great, this morning Tim, all morning about Jesus.

298
01:16:34.510 --> 01:16:37.510
He almost said, we are nothing and Jesus is everything.

299
01:16:37.510 --> 01:16:40.510
And that is more or less true too.

300
01:16:40.510 --> 01:16:43.510
Or maybe completely true.

301
01:16:43.510 --> 01:16:50.510
And then it was nine o'clock and Vanessa closed the evening.

302
01:16:50.510 --> 01:16:56.510
Once again with the words, not as a song, but just to conclude.

303
01:16:56.510 --> 01:16:58.510
Jesus is Lord.

304
01:16:58.510 --> 01:17:00.510
Jesus is the head.

305
01:17:00.510 --> 01:17:02.510
Jesus is our leader.

306
01:17:02.510 --> 01:17:08.510
So, let us never forget that when we talk about the body.

307
01:17:08.510 --> 01:17:10.510
That it all revolves around Jesus.

308
01:17:10.510 --> 01:17:13.510
And we do it for Jesus and we do it through Jesus.

309
01:17:13.510 --> 01:17:17.510
And Jesus, I want to thank You that You are our head.

310
01:17:17.510 --> 01:17:20.510
I want to thank You that You are our leader.

311
01:17:20.510 --> 01:17:25.510
If we had to do it out of our own wisdom, we wouldn't get far.

312
01:17:25.510 --> 01:17:30.510
But I thank You, Lord, that You have all wisdom and all love and all power and strength

313
01:17:30.510 --> 01:17:33.510
and majesty and authority, Lord.

314
01:17:33.510 --> 01:17:35.510
To lead Your congregation well.

315
01:17:35.510 --> 01:17:38.510
Hallelujah, we love You, Jesus.

316
01:17:39.510 --> 01:17:44.510
By the way, it's beautiful how the Spirit speaks.

317
01:17:44.510 --> 01:17:51.510
That the last words I heard this morning before the service began were

318
01:17:51.510 --> 01:17:53.510
Everyone has their gifts.

319
01:17:53.510 --> 01:18:02.510
Kitty said to me, aren't you nervous about standing on stage later?

320
01:18:02.510 --> 01:18:04.510
I said, no, it's not that bad.

321
01:18:04.510 --> 01:18:09.510
Well, she said, that wouldn't happen to me.

322
01:18:09.510 --> 01:18:11.510
And then she said, but, to each their own gifts.

323
01:18:11.510 --> 01:18:13.510
And those were the last words I heard.

324
01:18:13.510 --> 01:18:17.510
And that is exactly what we are going to talk about this morning together.

325
01:18:18.510 --> 01:18:22.510
It is so beautiful how the Spirit always speaks and confirms.

326
01:18:25.510 --> 01:18:31.510
So, Jesus is the head, we are the body, we are His hands and feet to do what He wants.

327
01:18:31.510 --> 01:18:33.510
But how does that work?

328
01:18:33.510 --> 01:18:39.510
How does God work in this congregation, how does God work through His body?

329
01:18:39.510 --> 01:18:46.510
Because, take a random group of people, like this bunch here.

330
01:18:47.510 --> 01:18:52.510
Put them in a building together and shake them up a bit.

331
01:18:52.510 --> 01:18:54.510
And then see what happens.

332
01:18:55.510 --> 01:18:58.510
Because, how different are we all?

333
01:18:58.510 --> 01:19:01.510
With the different talents that we have.

334
01:19:01.510 --> 01:19:03.510
The characters that we have.

335
01:19:03.510 --> 01:19:06.510
One shines a bit more than the other.

336
01:19:07.510 --> 01:19:10.510
People make mistakes when they interact with each other.

337
01:19:10.510 --> 01:19:13.510
They hurt and grieve each other.

338
01:19:14.510 --> 01:19:17.510
People disagree with each other.

339
01:19:18.510 --> 01:19:20.510
They do not agree with each other.

340
01:19:20.510 --> 01:19:23.510
People are opinionated, they know better.

341
01:19:24.510 --> 01:19:29.510
People are cutting corners and letting others do the work.

342
01:19:30.510 --> 01:19:36.510
So how is God to build His body and His kingdom with us humans?

343
01:19:37.510 --> 01:19:41.510
Let's turn together to 1 Corinthians 12 verse 12.

344
01:19:42.510 --> 01:19:45.510
Debbie, may I have my bottle of water after all?

345
01:19:45.510 --> 01:19:49.510
I had said it wasn't necessary, but it is necessary.

346
01:19:56.510 --> 01:19:57.510
Thank you.

347
01:20:12.510 --> 01:20:19.510
For a body is one whole, but consists of different body parts.

348
01:20:19.510 --> 01:20:23.510
All those body parts together form one body.

349
01:20:23.510 --> 01:20:25.510
So it is with Christ.

350
01:20:26.510 --> 01:20:29.510
For we have all been baptized in one Spirit.

351
01:20:29.510 --> 01:20:32.510
So that we became one body together.

352
01:20:33.510 --> 01:20:37.510
It doesn't matter whether we are Jews or from another nation.

353
01:20:38.510 --> 01:20:49.510
Vanessa, there is again such a verse that shows how we, together with the Jewish people, are one people of God.

354
01:20:49.510 --> 01:20:55.510
For it also states here, we are together with the Jews one body.

355
01:20:56.510 --> 01:20:58.510
One body, not two bodies.

356
01:20:59.510 --> 01:21:05.510
And I am doing this together with my brothers and sisters at this moment also for Israel.

357
01:21:05.510 --> 01:21:11.510
The Jews in Jerusalem, in Israel, and scattered all over the world.

358
01:21:11.510 --> 01:21:15.510
Lord, I thank You that You join us together with them, Lord.

359
01:21:15.510 --> 01:21:18.510
That we are one body for You together.

360
01:21:18.510 --> 01:21:23.510
That we will worship Jesus together for eternity. Hallelujah.

361
01:21:24.510 --> 01:21:28.510
So it doesn't matter whether we are Jews or from another nation.

362
01:21:28.510 --> 01:21:32.510
It also doesn't matter whether we are slaves or free people.

363
01:21:32.510 --> 01:21:35.510
We are all filled with the same spirit.

364
01:21:38.510 --> 01:21:44.510
A body does not consist of just one part, but of many parts.

365
01:21:45.510 --> 01:21:52.510
If one of the feet were to say, 'Because I am not a hand, I do not belong to the body,' would it be right?

366
01:21:53.510 --> 01:22:00.510
And if an ear were to say, 'Because I am not an eye, I do not belong to the body,' would it be right?

367
01:22:01.510 --> 01:22:05.510
For how can a body hear if it only consists of eyes?

368
01:22:05.510 --> 01:22:11.510
And how can it smell if it only consists of ears?

369
01:22:12.510 --> 01:22:13.510
Just imagine.

370
01:22:14.510 --> 01:22:22.510
But God has given everyone their own special place in the body, where He wants.

371
01:22:22.510 --> 01:22:25.510
God determines. God is the head.

372
01:22:26.510 --> 01:22:33.510
He determines, it says here, each one a special place.

373
01:22:34.510 --> 01:22:41.510
It is not so much what you consider important or where you would want to function.

374
01:22:41.510 --> 01:22:44.510
Not even what you consider important.

375
01:22:44.510 --> 01:22:51.510
It is not so much what you consider important or where you would want to function.

376
01:22:51.510 --> 01:22:57.510
Not even what Tim considers important, although God obviously works through Tim.

377
01:22:58.510 --> 01:23:05.510
But it is God who made you, who gave you talent,

378
01:23:05.510 --> 01:23:11.510
who has destined you for a special place in the midst of the congregation.

379
01:23:15.510 --> 01:23:24.510
If we were all one body part, then it would not be a body.

380
01:23:26.510 --> 01:23:32.510
I can't help but talk about football with you now that the European Championship is going on.

381
01:23:32.510 --> 01:23:34.510
Where I am a big fan of.

382
01:23:35.510 --> 01:23:40.510
Imagine a football team, what is the most important thing that happens?

383
01:23:41.510 --> 01:23:42.510
Scoring goals.

384
01:23:42.510 --> 01:23:47.510
So who can score the best goal? The striker.

385
01:23:47.510 --> 01:23:53.510
So let's put eleven people on the field, eleven strikers on the field.

386
01:23:53.510 --> 01:23:54.510
Most of those goals.

387
01:23:55.510 --> 01:23:59.510
But wait, the opponent is going to try that too, of course.

388
01:23:59.510 --> 01:24:01.510
So a goalkeeper might also be handy.

389
01:24:01.510 --> 01:24:04.510
You know what? Eleven, ten strikers and one goalkeeper.

390
01:24:05.510 --> 01:24:13.510
You understand, that team that would do that is not going to win the European Championship, of course.

391
01:24:13.510 --> 01:24:19.510
Even the team with the best players in the world is not necessarily going to become champions.

392
01:24:20.510 --> 01:24:24.510
Which team is going to win the European Championship this year?

393
01:24:24.510 --> 01:24:30.510
That is the team where the right people, with the right specialties,

394
01:24:31.510 --> 01:24:33.510
are exactly in the right place.

395
01:24:33.510 --> 01:24:37.510
And not only that, they work perfectly together.

396
01:24:37.510 --> 01:24:42.510
That they adhere to the agreements that the coach has made.

397
01:24:43.510 --> 01:24:46.510
That team is going to win the European Championship. You will see.

398
01:24:46.510 --> 01:24:48.510
Because that's how it works.

399
01:24:48.510 --> 01:24:53.510
That's how it works in the kingdom of goals and that's how it works in a football team as well.

400
01:24:54.510 --> 01:24:56.510
So you shouldn't all...

401
01:24:56.510 --> 01:25:01.510
I think that most boys, how was it with Joshua?

402
01:25:01.510 --> 01:25:05.510
When they go to soccer, they all want to be strikers, right?

403
01:25:05.510 --> 01:25:09.510
Yes, that makes sense, because they score the goals.

404
01:25:09.510 --> 01:25:12.510
But you shouldn't all want to be strikers.

405
01:25:12.510 --> 01:25:16.510
You should stand where God made you to be.

406
01:25:16.510 --> 01:25:19.510
Where you are best at. Even in soccer.

407
01:25:20.510 --> 01:25:23.510
Let's continue with verse 20.

408
01:25:28.510 --> 01:25:33.510
But now there are many parts, yet one body.

409
01:25:35.510 --> 01:25:39.510
An eye cannot say to a hand, I don't need you.

410
01:25:39.510 --> 01:25:44.510
And the head cannot say to the feet, I don't need you.

411
01:25:45.510 --> 01:25:49.510
Imagine, where is Roy, the drummer?

412
01:25:50.510 --> 01:25:54.510
What do you call those sticks that you always hit the drums with?

413
01:25:55.510 --> 01:25:57.510
Drumsticks.

414
01:25:58.510 --> 01:26:00.510
How hard can it be?

415
01:26:00.510 --> 01:26:05.510
I was thinking of drumsticks, but I thought, you put those on the barbecue.

416
01:26:06.510 --> 01:26:08.510
Maybe it's called something else.

417
01:26:08.510 --> 01:26:13.510
Okay, suppose Roy, who is good with those drumsticks,

418
01:26:13.510 --> 01:26:19.510
suppose he starts drumming on the barbecue to make nice meat for Tim.

419
01:26:20.510 --> 01:26:22.510
That won't work.

420
01:26:22.510 --> 01:26:28.510
Or suppose Oscar starts banging on Chris's guitar with his barbecue fork.

421
01:26:28.510 --> 01:26:31.510
to create enjoyable worship.

422
01:26:31.510 --> 01:26:35.510
Or suppose Chris is going to mow the grass with his guitar.

423
01:26:35.510 --> 01:26:37.510
That won't get done very quickly either.

424
01:26:37.510 --> 01:26:41.510
Or Frans comes here to vacuum the stage with his lawnmower.

425
01:26:43.510 --> 01:26:48.510
So everyone has their own talent and things they are good at.

426
01:26:48.510 --> 01:26:54.510
And it is important that you use that in the place where it can best come to fruition.

427
01:26:55.510 --> 01:27:00.510
So you can't say, you are not needed, I will do it myself.

428
01:27:00.510 --> 01:27:02.510
I can't do that.

429
01:27:02.510 --> 01:27:06.510
I am not needed, I will do it myself. I can do that much better.

430
01:27:06.510 --> 01:27:08.510
You shouldn't do that at all.

431
01:27:10.510 --> 01:27:13.510
Let God determine who stands where.

432
01:27:13.510 --> 01:27:15.510
Verse 22.

433
01:27:15.510 --> 01:27:21.510
No, the parts of the body that seem the most vulnerable are the most necessary.

434
01:27:22.510 --> 01:27:27.510
And the parts of the body that we do not like to show, we adorn beautifully.

435
01:27:27.510 --> 01:27:33.510
The body parts that are not suitable to be shown, we keep covered.

436
01:27:33.510 --> 01:27:38.510
But the body parts that we can simply show, do not need that.

437
01:27:38.510 --> 01:27:48.510
And God has made the body in such a way that He has given an important task to the parts that seem unimportant.

438
01:27:48.510 --> 01:27:53.510
Now we are talking about important, unimportant.

439
01:27:53.510 --> 01:27:56.510
And that is something that is in all of us.

440
01:27:56.510 --> 01:28:00.510
We all want to be found important.

441
01:28:00.510 --> 01:28:03.510
Therefore, we also want to be in the spotlight.

442
01:28:06.510 --> 01:28:09.510
But God says something very different here.

443
01:28:09.510 --> 01:28:13.510
Things may seem unimportant and yet be very important.

444
01:28:13.510 --> 01:28:16.510
Only those may not stand out to people.

445
01:28:16.510 --> 01:28:18.510
But they do to God.

446
01:28:18.510 --> 01:28:20.510
The disciples had that too.

447
01:28:20.510 --> 01:28:24.510
When they walked with Jesus, they approached Jesus multiple times.

448
01:28:24.510 --> 01:28:30.510
From Jesus, may I later sit next to you who is on the throne.

449
01:28:30.510 --> 01:28:33.510
Because they found that to be very important.

450
01:28:33.510 --> 01:28:38.510
That they were so important that they could sit with Jesus.

451
01:28:38.510 --> 01:28:41.510
They asked him that multiple times.

452
01:28:41.510 --> 01:28:45.510
Moreover, they even sent their mothers to Jesus.

453
01:28:45.510 --> 01:28:48.510
To let those mothers ask Jesus.

454
01:28:48.510 --> 01:28:51.510
My son may sit next to you later, right?

455
01:28:51.510 --> 01:28:55.510
But there is something in us that wants to be important.

456
01:28:55.510 --> 01:28:58.510
But you are not important if you stand out to people.

457
01:28:58.510 --> 01:29:01.510
You are important if you stand out to God.

458
01:29:04.510 --> 01:29:07.510
And every task is important.

459
01:29:08.510 --> 01:29:12.510
So never seek the most important task.

460
01:29:12.510 --> 01:29:14.510
Or something that stands out the most.

461
01:29:14.510 --> 01:29:18.510
Or even something that people see you for and will compliment you on.

462
01:29:18.510 --> 01:29:20.510
I know that we have a need for that.

463
01:29:20.510 --> 01:29:22.510
But seek God.

464
01:29:22.510 --> 01:29:24.510
Seek to do what God wants.

465
01:29:26.510 --> 01:29:31.510
We just read, God has a specific place for you.

466
01:29:31.510 --> 01:29:35.510
So do not seek something else, but seek that specific place.

467
01:29:37.510 --> 01:29:41.510
So there is an order of God.

468
01:29:41.510 --> 01:29:43.510
In whom truth stands.

469
01:29:43.510 --> 01:29:45.510
There is only one pastor.

470
01:29:50.510 --> 01:29:56.510
Never confuse the order of God with importance.

471
01:29:59.510 --> 01:30:03.510
For that is not how God thinks, that is not how God looks.

472
01:30:03.510 --> 01:30:08.510
It is not a hierarchy of which position you take.

473
01:30:08.510 --> 01:30:13.510
If you are in the place where God wants you to be, then you are exactly right.

474
01:30:13.510 --> 01:30:15.510
Then God is pleased with you.

475
01:30:15.510 --> 01:30:18.510
Anyway, every person is precious.

476
01:30:18.510 --> 01:30:20.510
Extremely precious.

477
01:30:20.510 --> 01:30:24.510
Jesus gave his own life away because he finds you important.

478
01:30:24.510 --> 01:30:26.510
Because he wants to know you.

479
01:30:26.510 --> 01:30:31.510
Because he wants to place you where he made you for.

480
01:30:31.510 --> 01:30:37.510
Of which he so desires that you are and function and bear fruit for him.

481
01:30:37.510 --> 01:30:39.510
And then you are not precious.

482
01:30:39.510 --> 01:30:43.510
That could be cleaning the toilets or whatever.

483
01:30:43.510 --> 01:30:45.510
If God calls you to that.

484
01:30:45.510 --> 01:30:47.510
It may sound a bit silly.

485
01:30:47.510 --> 01:30:49.510
But wherever God calls you.

486
01:30:49.510 --> 01:30:55.510
If you do it there, you are just as important as the pastor or anyone else.

487
01:30:56.510 --> 01:30:59.510
And even when we will stand before God's throne later.

488
01:30:59.510 --> 01:31:01.510
We will be held accountable.

489
01:31:01.510 --> 01:31:03.510
As far as we are held accountable.

490
01:31:03.510 --> 01:31:08.510
But we will be judged by God on this.

491
01:31:08.510 --> 01:31:10.510
What have we done?

492
01:31:10.510 --> 01:31:13.510
God has destined us for a place in the congregation.

493
01:31:13.510 --> 01:31:15.510
And what have you done with that?

494
01:31:15.510 --> 01:31:18.510
The Bible also says, if much has been given to you.

495
01:31:18.510 --> 01:31:21.510
You will also be held to much account.

496
01:31:21.510 --> 01:31:24.510
If little has been given to you, you will be held to little account.

497
01:31:24.510 --> 01:31:29.510
So it is not necessarily because someone is in a so-called high position.

498
01:31:29.510 --> 01:31:32.510
That they are doing super well.

499
01:31:32.510 --> 01:31:35.510
And you who are doing a seemingly insignificant task for people.

500
01:31:35.510 --> 01:31:39.510
But doing it with all your heart and dedication and love for Jesus.

501
01:31:39.510 --> 01:31:45.510
How God will judge that.

502
01:31:49.510 --> 01:31:52.510
We also have many people in our church.

503
01:31:52.510 --> 01:31:54.510
I have been here for a while.

504
01:31:54.510 --> 01:31:57.510
We have so many faithful people here.

505
01:31:57.510 --> 01:32:00.510
Who have taken their position.

506
01:32:00.510 --> 01:32:03.510
Who do all kinds of work in this church.

507
01:32:03.510 --> 01:32:06.510
And who do that faithfully, year in and year out.

508
01:32:06.510 --> 01:32:08.510
And who do not stand out to anyone.

509
01:32:08.510 --> 01:32:11.510
When we stand here on the stage, we stand out.

510
01:32:11.510 --> 01:32:13.510
And oh, they are on the stage.

511
01:32:13.510 --> 01:32:15.510
And they are important.

512
01:32:15.510 --> 01:32:16.510
But I want to thank you.

513
01:32:16.510 --> 01:32:19.510
All the people who dedicate themselves to Jesus.

514
01:32:19.510 --> 01:32:23.510
And who receive little compliments or fame or honor.

515
01:32:23.510 --> 01:32:29.510
I want to thank you for your faithfulness, your dedicated service, and love for Jesus.

516
01:32:31.510 --> 01:32:37.510
And I could mention many names.

517
01:32:37.510 --> 01:32:39.510
Actually, I would love to do that.

518
01:32:39.510 --> 01:32:43.510
Because those people also need to be honored.

519
01:32:43.510 --> 01:32:45.510
And to be loved and recognized.

520
01:32:45.510 --> 01:32:49.510
Only if I start naming names, I will surely forget someone.

521
01:32:49.510 --> 01:32:51.510
So I'm just not going to do that.

522
01:32:51.510 --> 01:32:53.510
But really, thank you.

523
01:32:53.510 --> 01:32:55.510
Thank you for your faithfulness.

524
01:32:55.510 --> 01:32:58.510
We will continue with verse 25.

525
01:33:00.510 --> 01:33:04.510
Did you see Tim, how big the letters I printed were?

526
01:33:06.510 --> 01:33:09.510
Now I can barely read it without my glasses.

527
01:33:09.510 --> 01:33:13.510
I just don't feel like constantly taking my glasses on and off.

528
01:33:13.510 --> 01:33:15.510
Then my big letters.

529
01:33:15.510 --> 01:33:19.510
This way there is no division in the body.

530
01:33:19.510 --> 01:33:23.510
And all the members take good care of each other.

531
01:33:24.510 --> 01:33:27.510
No division in the body.

532
01:33:27.510 --> 01:33:29.510
So important.

533
01:33:30.510 --> 01:33:34.510
And that is, we live in a society where everyone has an opinion.

534
01:33:34.510 --> 01:33:38.510
And 16 million national coaches in the Netherlands.

535
01:33:38.510 --> 01:33:42.510
And everyone knows how it should be done better than the national coach.

536
01:33:42.510 --> 01:33:45.510
And then the government and then the pastor.

537
01:33:45.510 --> 01:33:49.510
But it is so important that we are one with each other.

538
01:33:49.510 --> 01:33:52.510
One of heart, one of soul, one of spirit.

539
01:33:52.510 --> 01:33:57.510
And just imagine that each of us has an arrow above our head.

540
01:33:57.510 --> 01:33:59.510
And it points in one direction.

541
01:34:00.510 --> 01:34:03.510
So we all have an arrow above our heads.

542
01:34:03.510 --> 01:34:08.510
And it points in the direction that we believe the congregation should go.

543
01:34:08.510 --> 01:34:14.510
What would it be like if all those arrows here pointed in different directions?

544
01:34:14.510 --> 01:34:19.510
And one starts pushing that way while the other starts pulling this way.

545
01:34:19.510 --> 01:34:22.510
Where is the congregation then headed?

546
01:34:22.510 --> 01:34:27.510
It just keeps going around in a little circle or something.

547
01:34:27.510 --> 01:34:32.510
But what happens when all our arrows point in the same direction?

548
01:34:32.510 --> 01:34:35.510
Wow, then something is going to happen.

549
01:34:35.510 --> 01:34:37.510
And that is what God wants.

550
01:34:37.510 --> 01:34:47.510
When we are united, take our position, and do what our pastor directs the congregation to do.

551
01:34:47.510 --> 01:34:50.510
Then something will happen like at the Tower of Babel.

552
01:34:50.510 --> 01:34:57.510
That when people go in the same direction in unity, nothing is impossible for them.

553
01:34:57.510 --> 01:35:03.510
And that is why God had to stop it in Babel, because they were not doing God's work at all.

554
01:35:03.510 --> 01:35:12.510
But let us be united, go in the same direction, following Jesus, following our pastor.

555
01:35:12.510 --> 01:35:15.510
Verse 26

556
01:35:15.510 --> 01:35:20.510
If one member suffers, all the others share in his suffering.

557
01:35:20.510 --> 01:35:25.510
If one member is honored, all the others rejoice with him.

558
01:35:25.510 --> 01:35:31.510
So important, we must be there for each other as a congregation.

559
01:35:31.510 --> 01:35:43.510
It should not be the case that if someone is in pain or struggling, dealing with their marriage or health or work or finances or anything else,

560
01:35:43.510 --> 01:35:51.510
that they stand alone while we are here with a few hundred people, but he or she feels so alone.

561
01:35:51.510 --> 01:35:53.510
That should not be the case.

562
01:35:53.510 --> 01:35:57.510
Give the verse, we need to empathize with one another, we need to stand up for each other,

563
01:35:57.510 --> 01:36:02.510
we need to encourage one another, we also need to correct each other where necessary,

564
01:36:02.510 --> 01:36:06.510
we need to help each other further, we especially need to pray for one another.

565
01:36:13.510 --> 01:36:15.510
Verse 27

566
01:36:15.510 --> 01:36:25.510
So you are together the body of Christ and each of you is a part of that body.

567
01:36:25.510 --> 01:36:32.510
One body, one congregation, this congregation.

568
01:36:32.510 --> 01:36:38.510
And I want to make a call to join the congregation.

569
01:36:38.510 --> 01:36:43.510
Maybe you are a visitor or you feel like a guest and that's fine in itself,

570
01:36:43.510 --> 01:36:50.510
but do not remain as a guest or visitor here on Sunday morning, but join in.

571
01:36:50.510 --> 01:36:58.510
We have just read that God has determined a specific place for all of us in the congregation.

572
01:36:58.510 --> 01:37:02.510
So seek it out and take that place.

573
01:37:02.510 --> 01:37:05.510
Be part of the congregation.

574
01:37:05.510 --> 01:37:10.510
We do not have official membership here,

575
01:37:10.510 --> 01:37:15.510
but that does not mean we cannot be members of this congregation,

576
01:37:15.510 --> 01:37:21.510
or better said of this body, because a member is an old word for a part of the body,

577
01:37:21.510 --> 01:37:24.510
which we have been talking about all this time.

578
01:37:24.510 --> 01:37:28.510
So be a member, be a part of this congregation.

579
01:37:28.510 --> 01:37:30.510
Join us.

580
01:37:30.510 --> 01:37:33.510
Let us build God's kingdom together.

581
01:37:33.510 --> 01:37:41.510
Do not go from congregation to congregation in search of where you are best fed or where you feel the most comfortable,

582
01:37:41.510 --> 01:37:47.510
but you do not have to be in this congregation, go to the congregation where you feel

583
01:37:47.510 --> 01:37:53.510
that God has called you to take your place there.

584
01:37:53.510 --> 01:37:57.510
And be faithful there through thick and thin, no matter what happens.

585
01:37:57.510 --> 01:38:02.510
Storms will come in your life, storms will come in the congregation.

586
01:38:02.510 --> 01:38:09.510
We are people together who must do this together with all our differences and do not always agree,

587
01:38:09.510 --> 01:38:12.510
and so on and so forth, but keep going.

588
01:38:12.510 --> 01:38:16.510
We live in a society where there is so little faithfulness.

589
01:38:16.510 --> 01:38:22.510
People change jobs every year, people give up their marriage when it is no longer fun.

590
01:38:22.510 --> 01:38:25.510
In such a society we live where faithfulness is hard to find.

591
01:38:25.510 --> 01:38:33.510
But I have learned that if you keep going in your work when it gets tough, in your marriage when it gets tough,

592
01:38:33.510 --> 01:38:40.510
yes, then you have a hard time, but I have learned and discovered with Chris together in our business

593
01:38:40.510 --> 01:38:46.510
and with Anja together in my marriage, that if you keep going, it only gets better afterwards.

594
01:38:46.510 --> 01:38:50.510
This is simply how God made it.

595
01:38:50.510 --> 01:38:53.510
He has given thorns and thistles.

596
01:38:53.510 --> 01:38:59.510
We need that. If everything were just smooth and fun and nice and we only looked

597
01:38:59.510 --> 01:39:03.510
for the fun things to do and picked the raisins out of the pudding, then it would not go well with us.

598
01:39:03.510 --> 01:39:09.510
Then we forget God, then we stray, and then it ends completely wrong.

599
01:39:09.510 --> 01:39:20.510
But if you are faithful, if you are faithful to your wife, to your work, to your congregation, to the government,

600
01:39:20.510 --> 01:39:26.510
then it will go well with you, you will be blessed, and God's kingdom will be advanced.

601
01:39:26.510 --> 01:39:33.510
So join in. Don't be a spectator, don't be a church helper, but join in.

602
01:39:33.510 --> 01:39:38.510
Get involved, take the place that God has determined for you.

603
01:39:43.510 --> 01:39:46.510
May I have the slide on the screen?

604
01:39:51.510 --> 01:40:00.510
You may not think about it much, but in a congregation like this, a lot happens.

605
01:40:03.510 --> 01:40:13.510
Debbie just said to me that in this congregation, the financial side, the entire bookkeeping and administration

606
01:40:13.510 --> 01:40:18.510
is a lot larger than at an average high school.

607
01:40:18.510 --> 01:40:23.510
And that's just one little thing, because here you see all kinds of teams.

608
01:40:23.510 --> 01:40:33.510
There are more than twenty specific teams that we have in our church to get everything organized practically.

609
01:40:33.510 --> 01:40:39.510
Because behind that stands the leader of each team and we obviously have pastors, Tim and Vanessa.

610
01:40:39.510 --> 01:40:45.510
We have an elder team with Bram and Els, we have a board with a number of people

611
01:40:46.510 --> 01:40:54.510
and then we also have quite a few teams that are more involved in the pastoral area,

612
01:40:54.510 --> 01:41:00.510
the prophetic worship, prayer area, but also a lot of practical things,

613
01:41:00.510 --> 01:41:06.510
such as the management of this building, the bookshop, the kitchen, the garden.

614
01:41:06.510 --> 01:41:13.510
So a lot is happening and once again, heartfelt thanks to everyone who is committed to that.

615
01:41:14.510 --> 01:41:20.510
Three camps are also coming up, where a lot of help is needed.

616
01:41:20.510 --> 01:41:26.510
Youth camp, young adults camp or children's camp, to be more precise, and men's camp.

617
01:41:26.510 --> 01:41:34.510
What we need are people to clean, night watch, drivers, cooking, setup and teardown.

618
01:41:34.510 --> 01:41:40.510
I always mention teardown, but teardown does sound a bit nicer.

619
01:41:41.510 --> 01:41:47.510
But there is a lot of work to be done in such a congregation and the great thing is, that is just possible.

620
01:41:47.510 --> 01:41:55.510
Because God has brought us all together here and everyone has received a talent or multiple talents from God.

621
01:41:55.510 --> 01:41:59.510
As we all go and do what God has made us for.

622
01:41:59.510 --> 01:42:06.510
Then the congregation grows and flourishes, and His kingdom advances, and through the congregation, people discover Jesus.

623
01:42:07.510 --> 01:42:11.510
So, what is the calling on your life?

624
01:42:11.510 --> 01:42:15.510
What is that specific place of yours?

625
01:42:15.510 --> 01:42:18.510
What has God made you for?

626
01:42:18.510 --> 01:42:30.510
Well, that's not something that on day one when you come to repentance, you receive a note from heaven with your name on it saying this is what you should do.

627
01:42:30.510 --> 01:42:35.510
No, that's something you have to grow into.

628
01:42:36.510 --> 01:42:44.510
And some tasks can be done by almost anyone, which again does not indicate that they are any less important.

629
01:42:44.510 --> 01:42:50.510
But some tasks, especially in the other teams, you can't just join like that.

630
01:42:50.510 --> 01:42:59.510
That's only logical, right? You can't just stand on the stage and talk about God if you've just been converted because you don't know anything about God yet.

631
01:42:59.510 --> 01:43:07.510
For many tasks, it's important that you build a deep relationship with Jesus.

632
01:43:07.510 --> 01:43:17.510
That you read a lot in the Bible, that you pray, that you come to the services, that you come to the Monday evenings, that you come to prayer at a quarter to ten.

633
01:43:17.510 --> 01:43:37.510
That you participate and just be there and serve and help and be active, and then God, whether through Tim or other leaders or directly through revelations or prophecies you receive,

634
01:43:37.510 --> 01:43:43.510
will show you what your place is, what He has destined you for.

635
01:43:44.510 --> 01:43:54.510
So if you think you can easily get away with it and just sit in your chair waiting to be placed in that spot for which God made you, that will never work.

636
01:43:57.510 --> 01:43:59.510
Roll up your sleeves.

637
01:44:00.510 --> 01:44:10.510
And then you might say, yes, but I know my calling and I know what I am going to do.

638
01:44:10.510 --> 01:44:19.510
That is very important, and I will wait as long as it takes until I can do that in the church because that is my task. I won't do anything else.

639
01:44:20.510 --> 01:44:28.510
But when I had just been converted, I came across this text, and it helped me immensely.

640
01:44:28.510 --> 01:44:38.510
It is found in Ecclesiastes 9:10, and we will read it from the HSV because it is translated a bit less conveniently in the Basic Bible.

641
01:44:39.510 --> 01:44:49.510
Although I find the Basic Bible a beautiful Bible, when it comes to theological matters, it is good not to stay with the Basic Bible,

642
01:44:49.510 --> 01:44:53.510
but also to look at other translations of what is written there.

643
01:44:53.510 --> 01:45:03.510
For the Bible was originally written in Hebrew, Aramaic, and Greek, and all other versions are translations.

644
01:45:03.510 --> 01:45:14.510
So especially if you pick one verse from one translation, it can lead you to very different thoughts than what God actually meant there.

645
01:45:14.510 --> 01:45:17.510
Ecclesiastes 9 verse 10.

646
01:45:17.510 --> 01:45:23.510
Whatever your hand finds to do, do it according to your ability.

647
01:45:23.510 --> 01:45:28.510
Whatever your hand finds to do, do it according to your ability.

648
01:45:29.510 --> 01:45:37.510
In other words, you can sit in your chair until you can do what you think you are called to do,

649
01:45:37.510 --> 01:45:40.510
but in the meantime, a lot needs to happen.

650
01:45:40.510 --> 01:45:43.510
Like helping at the camps.

651
01:45:43.510 --> 01:45:46.510
And then the Bible says, do what your hand finds to do.

652
01:45:46.510 --> 01:45:51.510
In other words, if you see something that needs to be done in the congregation, then help out.

653
01:45:52.510 --> 01:45:56.510
Just do it and not just casually, because I will help a little.

654
01:45:56.510 --> 01:45:59.510
For it even says, do it according to your ability.

655
01:45:59.510 --> 01:46:02.510
In other words, do your best.

656
01:46:02.510 --> 01:46:07.510
If you see a piece of paper lying on the ground, pick it up.

657
01:46:07.510 --> 01:46:14.510
Just help with what you see is needed and do not wait for the most important task.

658
01:46:15.510 --> 01:46:21.510
Jesus gave the perfect example of this with the foot washing.

659
01:46:21.510 --> 01:46:26.510
It was almost the moment he was going to be nailed to the cross.

660
01:46:26.510 --> 01:46:30.510
He had his last meal together with his friends.

661
01:46:30.510 --> 01:46:32.510
And what does he start with?

662
01:46:32.510 --> 01:46:35.510
By washing the feet of the disciples.

663
01:46:35.510 --> 01:46:38.510
You have probably heard that story.

664
01:46:38.510 --> 01:46:40.510
But why does Jesus do that?

665
01:46:40.510 --> 01:46:42.510
Because it is so important.

666
01:46:42.510 --> 01:46:47.510
Wherever we are called, to be of service.

667
01:46:47.510 --> 01:46:52.510
To help, to put our shoulders to the wheel, to do what is necessary.

668
01:46:52.510 --> 01:47:02.510
If one of the other disciples had been so sneaky as to wash the feet of the rest, Jesus wouldn't have had to do it.

669
01:47:02.510 --> 01:47:04.510
Because he was there for something very different.

670
01:47:04.510 --> 01:47:08.510
He certainly did not come to wash people's feet, of course.

671
01:47:09.510 --> 01:47:11.510
But no one did it.

672
01:47:11.510 --> 01:47:14.510
And then Jesus did it.

673
01:47:14.510 --> 01:47:16.510
And this is how we should also approach it.

674
01:47:16.510 --> 01:47:20.510
If you see a gap in the congregation of something that no one is doing, which needs to be done.

675
01:47:20.510 --> 01:47:22.510
Just do it.

676
01:47:22.510 --> 01:47:24.510
Help out.

677
01:47:24.510 --> 01:47:34.510
Did you know that most of the work is done by a relatively small group of people?

678
01:47:34.510 --> 01:47:37.510
We are here with about 300 people.

679
01:47:38.510 --> 01:47:43.510
There may be only a few dozen who really put their shoulders to the wheel.

680
01:47:43.510 --> 01:47:46.510
And the rest does little or nothing.

681
01:47:46.510 --> 01:47:49.510
But that is not how God intended it at all.

682
01:47:49.510 --> 01:47:51.510
Join in.

683
01:47:51.510 --> 01:47:53.510
Put your shoulders to the wheel.

684
01:48:01.510 --> 01:48:05.510
But why does all that work actually need to be done?

685
01:48:05.510 --> 01:48:07.510
Is all of that really necessary?

686
01:48:07.510 --> 01:48:17.510
It does not say in the Bible that we are not saved by trying our best.

687
01:48:17.510 --> 01:48:20.510
Tim mentioned it again this morning.

688
01:48:20.510 --> 01:48:26.510
We can do absolutely nothing to be saved.

689
01:48:26.510 --> 01:48:29.510
So what is all that actually for?

690
01:48:29.510 --> 01:48:35.510
All those teams and all that work we put in are indeed necessary.

691
01:48:35.510 --> 01:48:43.510
And can't I just love Jesus and come to the service and pray and worship and participate?

692
01:48:43.510 --> 01:48:46.510
I think that's just fine.

693
01:48:46.510 --> 01:48:53.510
Well, you are not saved no matter how hard you try.

694
01:48:53.510 --> 01:48:56.510
That will not bring you salvation.

695
01:48:57.510 --> 01:49:05.510
There is nothing we can do to bridge the gap between God and us.

696
01:49:05.510 --> 01:49:09.510
There is nothing we can do to correct our sins.

697
01:49:09.510 --> 01:49:12.510
Absolutely nothing.

698
01:49:12.510 --> 01:49:15.510
That is completely true.

699
01:49:15.510 --> 01:49:19.510
But we are saved.

700
01:49:20.510 --> 01:49:26.510
Thanks to Jesus, Tim mentioned repeatedly this morning.

701
01:49:26.510 --> 01:49:30.510
Jesus has accomplished everything, therefore He is the head.

702
01:49:30.510 --> 01:49:33.510
He has ensured that everything will be alright.

703
01:49:33.510 --> 01:49:35.510
And we cannot add anything to that.

704
01:49:35.510 --> 01:49:38.510
So therefore you do not have to do your best.

705
01:49:38.510 --> 01:49:41.510
But we do need to do our best.

706
01:49:41.510 --> 01:49:43.510
So how does that work?

707
01:49:43.510 --> 01:49:46.510
Let us read in James 2 verse 17.

708
01:49:47.510 --> 01:49:51.510
Sorry, 17 and 18.

709
01:49:51.510 --> 01:49:53.510
And then I will jump to 26.

710
01:49:53.510 --> 01:49:55.510
The whole passage is about this.

711
01:49:55.510 --> 01:49:59.510
Only we do not have time to read all of it.

712
01:50:01.510 --> 01:50:04.510
So we will pick out three verses.

713
01:50:04.510 --> 01:50:07.510
In James 2 verse 17 it says.

714
01:50:07.510 --> 01:50:10.510
So it is with faith.

715
01:50:10.510 --> 01:50:14.510
Your faith must be evident in what you do.

716
01:50:17.510 --> 01:50:21.510
If it is not evident, then your faith is dead.

717
01:50:22.510 --> 01:50:24.510
You might respond.

718
01:50:24.510 --> 01:50:25.510
I have faith.

719
01:50:25.510 --> 01:50:27.510
I have faith.

720
01:50:27.510 --> 01:50:29.510
You do good things.

721
01:50:29.510 --> 01:50:31.510
We both do that.

722
01:50:32.510 --> 01:50:39.510
If that could really happen, then show me that you believe without doing anything.

723
01:50:39.510 --> 01:50:44.510
Then I will show you my faith by the things I do.

724
01:50:44.510 --> 01:50:46.510
And then 26.

725
01:50:46.510 --> 01:50:49.510
Faith without deeds is dead.

726
01:50:49.510 --> 01:50:53.510
Just as a body without spirit is dead.

727
01:50:55.510 --> 01:51:00.510
And I thought this morning that Jesus said.

728
01:51:00.510 --> 01:51:05.510
Not everyone who says, Lord, Lord.

729
01:51:05.510 --> 01:51:08.510
But he who does the will of the Father.

730
01:51:08.510 --> 01:51:11.510
Will enter the kingdom.

731
01:51:12.510 --> 01:51:14.510
So that is very primary.

732
01:51:14.510 --> 01:51:16.510
So what's the deal?

733
01:51:16.510 --> 01:51:20.510
Do you have to work to be saved or not?

734
01:51:20.510 --> 01:51:23.510
No, you do not have to work to be saved.

735
01:51:23.510 --> 01:51:29.510
For only through the blood of Jesus do you find salvation and nothing else.

736
01:51:29.510 --> 01:51:35.510
But if you do not commit yourself to God's kingdom, where is your faith then?

737
01:51:35.510 --> 01:51:39.510
Then you might wonder if you even believe at all.

738
01:51:39.510 --> 01:51:41.510
For you can say, Lord, Lord.

739
01:51:41.510 --> 01:51:44.510
You can say, I love Jesus.

740
01:51:44.510 --> 01:51:47.510
You can participate in the worship.

741
01:51:47.510 --> 01:51:51.510
But if you do nothing, is it really true?

742
01:51:51.510 --> 01:51:55.510
Then you want to take the risk of standing before God later.

743
01:51:55.510 --> 01:51:58.510
And that God says, depart from me, for I never knew you.

744
01:51:58.510 --> 01:52:03.510
But, that's a bit of the negative approach.

745
01:52:03.510 --> 01:52:07.510
But the beautiful approach is, Jesus has done everything for us.

746
01:52:07.510 --> 01:52:10.510
He loves us so much.

747
01:52:10.510 --> 01:52:15.510
And he wants so badly to form his body, his bride, with us.

748
01:52:15.510 --> 01:52:17.510
And to be with us forever.

749
01:52:17.510 --> 01:52:23.510
And he wants as many people as possible in this world to find God's kingdom.

750
01:52:23.510 --> 01:52:24.510
To find Him.

751
01:52:24.510 --> 01:52:26.510
And to join in as well.

752
01:52:26.510 --> 01:52:30.510
So, shouldn't we, out of love for Jesus,

753
01:52:31.510 --> 01:52:37.510
align ourselves with the heart of Jesus, which beats for a lost world?

754
01:52:37.510 --> 01:52:43.510
Shouldn't we put our shoulders to the wheel and do our utmost?

755
01:52:43.510 --> 01:52:45.510
To build his kingdom.

756
01:52:45.510 --> 01:52:47.510
As he indicates.

757
01:52:51.510 --> 01:52:53.510
Yes, good timing.

758
01:52:53.510 --> 01:52:56.510
I was just about to say that you could come up on stage.

759
01:52:56.510 --> 01:52:58.510
Because we are almost closing.

760
01:53:01.510 --> 01:53:07.510
I want to close with Romans, chapter 25, verse 23.

761
01:53:11.510 --> 01:53:15.510
It is about the parable of the talents.

762
01:53:15.510 --> 01:53:19.510
You have probably heard of it as well.

763
01:53:19.510 --> 01:53:24.510
Jesus gives one five talents, another two, and another one.

764
01:53:24.510 --> 01:53:29.510
Or not Jesus, but he refers to a story of a landowner.

765
01:53:30.510 --> 01:53:33.510
And then he goes away for a long time.

766
01:53:33.510 --> 01:53:35.510
And then he comes back.

767
01:53:35.510 --> 01:53:42.510
And then he asks his servants what they have done with those talents.

768
01:53:44.510 --> 01:53:46.510
You might know it well.

769
01:53:46.510 --> 01:53:48.510
The first two have done well and good.

770
01:53:48.510 --> 01:53:51.510
